WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:05.850
What happens when you place a credit card
into SCP-914, or The Clockworks?

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.730
Dr. Naismith decided to find out.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.990
Dr. Naismith placed his credit card into SCP-914
on the setting "Very Fine."

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.970
The output was a similar-looking credit card,
printed with the phrase "RANK-ALEPH INFINITE

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:20.140
MONEY PRIVILEGES."

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.480
Dr. Naismith received a note reading:

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.930
"Dr. Naismith, I didn’t think I need to
remind you that SCP-914 is not to be used

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.310
for personal financial gain, but it seems
I was wrong.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.509
Consider this an official warning.

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:33.760
-Dr. Coltrane"

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.289
He placed the note itself into the Clockworks,
on the setting "Very Fine."

00:00:37.289 --> 00:00:41.739
The machinery produced a note that instead
read: "Dr. Naismith, I didn’t even think

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:47.500
of using SCP-914 for personal financial gain,
but that seems like a solid idea.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.449
Consider this official permission to reap
the fruits of your labor.

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:52.649
-O5-11”

